<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="dark">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>RECONCILIATION REQUIRED — Relational Amortization Registry & World Atlas</title>
    
    <!-- Tailwind CSS CDN -->
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <script>
        tailwind.config = {
            darkMode: 'class',
            theme: {
                extend: {
                    colors: {
                        basalt: {
                            900: '#0a0c0e',
                            800: '#121619',
                            700: '#1b2024',
                            600: '#283037',
                        },
                        teal: {
                            muted: '#2c4a4e',
                            glow: '#3d6b70',
                            deep: '#132326',
                        },
                        ochre: {
                            desert: '#c2925b',
                            dim: '#8a653a',
                            light: '#dfb27e',
                        },
                        chalk: '#e6e8e6',
                        amber: {
                            alert: '#d97706',
                            emergency: '#b45309',
                            pulse: '#f59e0b',
                        }
                    },
                    fontFamily: {
                        serif: ['Cinzel', 'Playfair Display', 'Georgia', 'serif'],
                        sans: ['Inter', 'Plus Jakarta Sans', 'sans-serif'],
                        mono: ['JetBrains Mono', 'Courier New', 'monospace'],
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    </script>
    
    <!-- Google Fonts -->
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cinzel:wght@400;600;800&family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@300;400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    
    <!-- Lucide Icons -->
    <script src="https://unpkg.com/lucide@latest"></script>

    <style>
        /* Custom scrollbar & film grain overlay */
        ::-webkit-scrollbar {
            width: 5px;
        }
        ::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
            background: #0a0c0e;
        }
        ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
            background: #283037;
            border-radius: 2px;
        }
        ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
            background: #c2925b;
        }

        .grain-overlay {
            position: fixed;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            width: 100vw;
            height: 100vh;
            pointer-events: none;
            z-index: 9999;
            opacity: 0.035;
            background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 200 200' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noiseFilter'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.8' numOctaves='3' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noiseFilter)'/%3E%3C/svg%3E");
        }

        .scanline {
            position: fixed;
            top: 0;
            left: 0;
            width: 100%;
            height: 100%;
            pointer-events: none;
            z-index: 9998;
            background: linear-gradient(
                to bottom,
                rgba(255,255,255,0),
                rgba(255,255,255,0) 50%,
                rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15) 50%,
                rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15)
            );
            background-size: 100% 4px;
            opacity: 0.4;
        }

        .cinematic-vignette {
            box-shadow: inset 0 0 150px rgba(0,0,0,0.85);
        }

        .glitch-hover:hover {
            text-shadow: 1px 0 0 rgba(194,146,91,0.5), -1px 0 0 rgba(44,74,78,0.5);
        }

        /* Reading Prose Typography Enhancements */
        .story-prose p {
            margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
            line-height: 1.9;
            font-size: 1.05rem;
            color: rgba(230, 232, 230, 0.88);
            font-weight: 300;
        }
        .story-prose p:first-of-type::first-letter {
            font-family: 'Cinzel', serif;
            font-size: 3.5rem;
            float: left;
            line-height: 0.8;
            margin-right: 0.75rem;
            color: #c2925b;
        }
        .story-prose strong {
            color: #e6e8e6;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        /* Map styling effects */
        .map-grid-bg {
            background-size: 40px 40px;
            background-image: 
                linear-gradient(to right, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03) 1px, transparent 1px),
                linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03) 1px, transparent 1px);
        }
        
        .map-marker {
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: transform 0.2s ease, filter 0.2s ease;
        }
        .map-marker:hover {
            transform: scale(1.25);
            filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.8));
        }

        .map-pulse {
            animation: pulse-ring 2s infinite cubic-bezier(0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);
        }

        @keyframes pulse-ring {
            0% { transform: scale(0.8); opacity: 0.8; }
            50% { transform: scale(1.6); opacity: 0; }
            100% { transform: scale(0.8); opacity: 0; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="bg-basalt-900 text-chalk font-sans antialiased selection:bg-ochre-desert selection:text-basalt-900 min-h-screen flex flex-col relative overflow-x-hidden">

    <div class="grain-overlay"></div>
    <div class="scanline"></div>

    <!-- Header / Navigation -->
    <header class="fixed top-0 left-0 w-full z-50 bg-basalt-900/80 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-basalt-700/60 transition-all duration-300">
        <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 h-16 sm:h-20 flex items-center justify-between">
            <div class="flex items-center space-x-3 cursor-pointer" onclick="showSection('hero')">
                <div class="w-3 h-3 bg-amber-alert animate-pulse rounded-full"></div>
                <div class="flex flex-col">
                    <span class="font-serif tracking-widest text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold uppercase text-chalk">AMORTIZATION AUTHORITY</span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-[9px] sm:text-[10px] text-ochre-desert/80 uppercase tracking-wider">SECTOR 04 // BUREAU OF BALANCE</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Desktop Nav -->
            <nav class="hidden lg:flex items-center space-x-6 text-xs font-mono tracking-widest uppercase">
                <button onclick="showSection('hero')" class="nav-link text-chalk/70 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors py-2" id="nav-hero">ARCHIVE HERO</button>
                <button onclick="showSection('story')" class="nav-link text-chalk/70 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors py-2" id="nav-story">STORY ARCHIVE</button>
                <button onclick="showSection('characters')" class="nav-link text-chalk/70 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors py-2" id="nav-characters">CHARACTER DOSSIERS</button>
                <button onclick="showSection('atlas')" class="nav-link text-chalk/70 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors py-2" id="nav-atlas">WORLD ATLAS</button>
                <button onclick="showSection('dossier')" class="nav-link text-chalk/70 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors py-2" id="nav-dossier">DOSSIERS & LOGS</button>
                <button onclick="showSection('calculator')" class="nav-link text-chalk/70 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors py-2" id="nav-calculator">DEBT AUDIT</button>
                <button onclick="showSection('codex')" class="nav-link text-chalk/70 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors py-2" id="nav-codex">CODEX</button>
            </nav>

            <div class="flex items-center space-x-4">
                <div class="hidden sm:flex flex-col text-right font-mono text-[10px] text-chalk/50">
                    <span>SECTOR STATUS: <span class="text-teal-glow">STABLE</span></span>
                    <span>PURGE CYCLE: <span class="text-amber-alert">14 DAYS</span></span>
                </div>
                <button id="mobile-menu-btn" class="lg:hidden text-chalk p-2 hover:text-ochre-desert" aria-label="Toggle menu">
                    <i data-lucide="menu" class="w-6 h-6"></i>
                </button>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Mobile Navigation Menu -->
        <div id="mobile-menu" class="hidden lg:hidden bg-basalt-800/95 border-b border-basalt-700 px-6 py-6 space-y-3 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest">
            <button onclick="showSection('hero'); toggleMobileMenu();" class="block w-full text-left py-2 border-b border-basalt-700 text-chalk">01 // Archive Hero</button>
            <button onclick="showSection('story'); toggleMobileMenu();" class="block w-full text-left py-2 border-b border-basalt-700 text-chalk">02 // Story Archive</button>
            <button onclick="showSection('characters'); toggleMobileMenu();" class="block w-full text-left py-2 border-b border-basalt-700 text-chalk">03 // Character Dossiers</button>
            <button onclick="showSection('atlas'); toggleMobileMenu();" class="block w-full text-left py-2 border-b border-basalt-700 text-ochre-desert font-bold">04 // World Atlas (Cartography)</button>
            <button onclick="showSection('dossier'); toggleMobileMenu();" class="block w-full text-left py-2 border-b border-basalt-700 text-chalk">05 // Dossiers & Logs</button>
            <button onclick="showSection('calculator'); toggleMobileMenu();" class="block w-full text-left py-2 border-b border-basalt-700 text-chalk">06 // Debt Audit Calculator</button>
            <button onclick="showSection('codex'); toggleMobileMenu();" class="block w-full text-left py-2 text-chalk">07 // Amortization Codex</button>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main class="flex-grow pt-16 sm:pt-20">
        
        <!-- SECTION: HERO -->
        <section id="section-hero" class="relative min-h-[calc(100vh-4rem)] flex flex-col justify-between p-6 sm:p-12 lg:p-20 overflow-hidden cinematic-vignette">
            <!-- Background Image with Dark Vignette Overlay -->
            <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?q=80&w=2000&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="Brutalist concrete infrastructure overtaken by moss and volcanic mist" class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center opacity-35 scale-105 transition-transform duration-10000 ease-out hover:scale-100" />
                <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-basalt-900 via-basalt-900/60 to-basalt-900/40"></div>
                <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-basalt-900/90 via-transparent to-basalt-900/90"></div>
            </div>

            <!-- Foreground Content -->
            <div class="relative z-10 max-w-5xl my-auto space-y-6 pt-12">
                <div class="inline-flex items-center space-x-3 bg-basalt-800/80 border border-basalt-600/60 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-sm">
                    <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-alert animate-ping"></span>
                    <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ochre-desert uppercase tracking-widest">CIVIC DISPATCH #409-B • STRICT CONFIDENTIALITY</span>
                </div>

                <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl tracking-tight font-extrabold text-chalk leading-none uppercase">
                    Reconciliation<br/>
                    <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-ochre-desert via-ochre-light to-chalk">Required</span>
                </h1>

                <p class="font-sans text-base sm:text-lg md:text-xl text-chalk/80 max-w-2xl font-light leading-relaxed">
                    In the island city of <span class="text-ochre-desert font-normal">Aethelgard</span>, emotional bonds are subject to state ledgering. Every intimacy creates an unpaid debt to the public framework. When debt balances exceed systemic tolerance, citizens undergo total Relational Amortization.
                </p>

                <div class="pt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-stretch sm:items-center space-y-4 sm:space-y-0 sm:space-x-6">
                    <button onclick="showSection('story')" class="group relative px-8 py-4 bg-ochre-desert text-basalt-900 font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest hover:bg-ochre-light transition-all shadow-lg flex items-center justify-center space-x-3">
                        <span>READ THE STORY ARCHIVE</span>
                        <i data-lucide="arrow-right" class="w-4 h-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1"></i>
                    </button>
                    
                    <button onclick="showSection('atlas')" class="px-8 py-4 border border-basalt-600 bg-basalt-800/50 backdrop-blur-sm text-chalk font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest hover:border-ochre-desert hover:text-ochre-desert transition-all text-center flex items-center justify-center space-x-2">
                        <i data-lucide="map" class="w-4 h-4 text-ochre-desert"></i>
                        <span>EXPLORE MUNICIPAL ATLAS</span>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Footer Ticker/Metadata -->
            <div class="relative z-10 pt-12 border-t border-basalt-700/50 grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6 font-mono text-xs text-chalk/50">
                <div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] uppercase text-ochre-desert/80">LOCATION</div>
                    <div class="text-chalk font-semibold mt-0.5">Basalt Basin • Sector 04</div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] uppercase text-ochre-desert/80">AMORTIZED TODAY</div>
                    <div class="text-chalk font-semibold mt-0.5">142 Citizens</div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] uppercase text-ochre-desert/80">MEMORY MONITORS</div>
                    <div class="text-teal-glow font-semibold mt-0.5">ACTIVE &amp; SCANNING</div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] uppercase text-ochre-desert/80">CIVIC LAW</div>
                    <div class="text-chalk font-semibold mt-0.5">DECREE 88-E (REVISED)</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SECTION: STORY ARCHIVE -->
        <section id="section-story" class="hidden min-h-screen relative bg-basalt-900">
            <!-- Persistent Act Progress Bar -->
            <div class="sticky top-16 sm:top-20 z-40 bg-basalt-900/90 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-basalt-700/80 px-4 py-3">
                <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-3 font-mono text-xs">
                    <div class="flex items-center space-x-2 text-ochre-desert">
                        <i data-lucide="book-open" class="w-4 h-4"></i>
                        <span class="uppercase tracking-widest font-semibold">STORY ARCHIVE</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex items-center space-x-2 sm:space-x-4">
                        <button onclick="scrollToAct('act-1')" id="act-btn-1" class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-basalt-700 text-chalk hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors">ACT I</button>
                        <button onclick="scrollToAct('act-2')" id="act-btn-2" class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-basalt-800 text-chalk/60 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors">ACT II</button>
                        <button onclick="scrollToAct('act-3')" id="act-btn-3" class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-basalt-800 text-chalk/60 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors">ACT III</button>
                        <button onclick="scrollToAct('act-4')" id="act-btn-4" class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-basalt-800 text-chalk/60 hover:text-ochre-desert transition-colors">ACT IV</button>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ACT I -->
            <article id="act-1" class="act-block border-b border-basalt-700/60 pb-20">
                <div class="relative h-[65vh] w-full flex items-end p-6 sm:p-12 lg:p-20 overflow-hidden">
                    <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509198397868-475647b2a1e5?q=80&w=2000&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="Brutalist basalt corridor reclaimed by tropical ferns and volcanic steam" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover opacity-40" />
                    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-basalt-900 via-basalt-900/50 to-transparent"></div>
                    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-4xl space-y-3">
                        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ochre-desert">// ACT I</span>
                        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-chalk uppercase font-bold">FRONTIER EROSION</h2>
                        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-chalk/60">SECTOR 04 // BASALT PERIMETER & LOGISTICS HUB</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8 pt-12 story-prose">
                    <p>
                        The volcanic rain in Sector 04 smelled faintly of copper and wet ash. Teo stood beneath the overhang of the transit gantry, tracing his thumb over a groove carved into the basalt column. Three years ago, he and Kian had gouged those twin initials into the stone with a discarded tungsten chisel. Today, the lines were shallow, smoothed down as if worn by decades of tide rather than thirty-six months of rain.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        He pulled out his field tablet, opening the perimeter log. The system registered no structural erosion on Column 14. Yet, when he pressed his palm flat against the stone, the notch felt almost entirely erased. It wasn't weathering. It was as if the stone itself was forgetting it had ever been marked.
                    </p>

                    <div class="my-8 p-4 sm:p-6 bg-black border border-amber-alert/40 rounded-sm font-mono text-xs space-y-2 text-amber-alert/90 shadow-xl">
                        <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-amber-alert/20 pb-2">
                            <span>[MUNICIPAL MONITOR FEED — WAREHOUSE 88]</span>
                            <span class="animate-pulse">STREAM: ANOMALOUS</span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-chalk/80">
                            &gt; LOG_ID: 884-DELTA<br>
                            &gt; RECONCILIATION AUDIT IN PROGRESS<br>
                            &gt; MATCHING ANTECEDENT RECORDS AGAINST CIVIC LEDGER 04...<br>
                            &gt; DISCREPANCY DETECTED: 1 RECORD UNREFERENCED.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <p>
                        Across the basin in the central logistics stack, Nadia stared at a dual monitor configuration in Warehouse 88. Her job was straightforward: catalog decommissioned domestic artifacts prior to physical incineration. On screen left, a feed showed a crate of leather-bound sketchbooks transferred from a residential unit in Sector 01. On screen right, the public index declared the unit had been vacant for nine years, assigned only to single-occupant industrial mechanics.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        She zoomed in on a handwritten note tucked inside the front cover of a sketch pad: <em>"Don't let them tell you the mist is natural."</em> Nadia checked the registry ID attached to the crate. The file returned a string of zeros. The name had already been scrubbed, but the ink remained.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Meanwhile, at the jungle perimeter where the basalt walls met the wild volcanic ridge, Priya walked the daily patrol line. Her thermal scanner hummed steadily, mapping dense tropical foliage against the perimeter grid. Halfway along fence line 12, her eyes caught a narrow path cutting straight through the ferns and banyan roots—a path clearly visible to the naked eye, yet completely absent from the LIDAR terrain map floating on her HUD.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        She stepped off the concrete apron onto the soft earth. The air grew immediately cooler, heavy with the scent of damp moss and ozone. The trail led directly toward a buried concrete archway half-swallowed by fig roots—an entrance that municipal records claimed was sealed during the original caldera stabilization forty years prior.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- ACT II -->
            <article id="act-2" class="act-block border-b border-basalt-700/60 pb-20">
                <div class="relative h-[65vh] w-full flex items-end p-6 sm:p-12 lg:p-20 overflow-hidden">
                    <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?q=80&w=2000&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="High security municipal archive vault in Aethelgard" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover opacity-40" />
                    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-basalt-900 via-basalt-900/50 to-transparent"></div>
                    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-4xl space-y-3">
                        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ochre-desert">// ACT II</span>
                        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-chalk uppercase font-bold">RECONCILIATION</h2>
                        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-chalk/60">SECTOR 00 // BUREAU OF RELATIONAL BALANCE</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8 pt-12 story-prose">
                    <p>
                        Yara sat inside the air-conditioned silence of the Bureau of Relational Balance. As a Senior Assessor, her screens displayed real-time emotional expenditure indices across all nine sectors. The math was immutable: every deep personal relationship created an unquantified liability against public stability. When two citizens built a private world, they withdrew emotional capacity from the state.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        A priority alert flashed gold on her central console. An automated amortization order had been queued for Case #7709-M. She clicked through to review the subject profile before authorizing neural dampening.
                    </p>

                    <div class="my-8 p-4 sm:p-6 bg-black border border-ochre-desert/50 rounded-sm font-mono text-xs space-y-2 text-ochre-desert shadow-xl">
                        <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-ochre-desert/20 pb-2">
                            <span>[CIVIC AMORTIZATION DOSSIER #7709-M]</span>
                            <span class="text-amber-alert font-bold">COUNTDOWN ACTIVE</span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-chalk/80">
                            &gt; SUBJECT NAME: KIAN VANCE<br>
                            &gt; ASSIGNED SISTER / CO-DEPENDENT: YARA VANCE<br>
                            &gt; ACCUMULATED RELATIONAL DEBT: 48,200 CR<br>
                            &gt; DISSOLUTION SCHEDULE: 02 HRS 14 MINS<br>
                            &gt; ACTION: TOTAL NEURAL AMORTIZATION & REALLOCATION
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <p>
                        Her breath hitched. Kian. Her brother's name wasn't supposed to appear in the high-deficit tier. They had taken every precaution—communicating only through brief, neutral municipal memos, keeping their living quarters separated by three transit sectors. But the system had detected an anomaly in their shared background data: a high-density memory node from their childhood in the volcanic rift settlements.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Yara opened the secret Relational Amortization Protocol sub-layer—a restricted ledger known only to high-ranking assessors. The protocol didn't just dampen memories; it actively redistributed the subjects' shared history into the island's geothermal power grid, converting human attachment into raw civic energy.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        If the countdown reached zero, Kian would not only forget her—he would cease to exist in every civic database, his identity erased from birth registries, medical logs, and housing assignments.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- ACT III -->
            <article id="act-3" class="act-block border-b border-basalt-700/60 pb-20">
                <div class="relative h-[65vh] w-full flex items-end p-6 sm:p-12 lg:p-20 overflow-hidden">
                    <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542273917363-3b1817f69a2d?q=80&w=2000&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="Ancient underground subterranean basalt machinery and roots" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover opacity-40" />
                    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-basalt-900 via-basalt-900/50 to-transparent"></div>
                    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-4xl space-y-3">
                        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ochre-desert">// ACT III</span>
                        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-chalk uppercase font-bold">CONVERGENCE</h2>
                        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-chalk/60">SUB-BASALT WELLS // ARCHIVAL MACHINERY</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8 pt-12 story-prose">
                    <p>
                        The sound of running water guided them deeper into the sub-basalt conduit. Nadia held her industrial lantern low, casting long shadows across massive bronze conduit pipes that ran parallel to the stone walls. Beside her, Teo checked the signal tracer he had adapted from a transit diagnostic unit.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        "The pipes aren't carrying thermal fluid," Nadia whispered, pointing to the frosted condensation along the heavy brass couplings. "It's liquid nitrogen. They're cooling something underneath the main reactor floor."
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Priya joined them at the junction, her military patrol gear coated in red volcanic mud. "The path outside leads directly down here," she said, shining her beam onto an ancient iron doorway set into the natural volcanic rock.
                    </p>

                    <div class="my-8 p-4 sm:p-6 bg-black border border-teal-glow/50 rounded-sm font-mono text-xs space-y-2 text-teal-glow shadow-xl">
                        <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-teal-glow/20 pb-2">
                            <span>[SUB-SILT SUBGRADE CHAMBER 00]</span>
                            <span>NODE STATUS: ACTIVE</span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-chalk/80">
                            &gt; PRIMARY RECEPTACLE: MEMORY COILS (4,000 TB CAPACITY)<br>
                            &gt; SYSTEM CORE: LIQUID NITROGEN COOLED AMORTIZATION WELL<br>
                            &gt; INCOMING DATA STREAM: SECTOR 04 RELATIONAL PURGE<br>
                            &gt; WARNING: UNAUTHORIZED PHYSICAL PRESENCE DETECTED.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <p>
                        They stepped through the portal into a colossal cavern illuminated by low-frequency teal indicator lights. Thousands of magnetic memory tiles hung from suspended circular racks, revolving slowly in vertical silos that extended down into the island's subterranean roots.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <!-- ACT IV -->
            <article id="act-4" class="act-block pb-20">
                <div class="relative h-[65vh] w-full flex items-end p-6 sm:p-12 lg:p-20 overflow-hidden">
                    <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1508739773434-c26b3d09e071?q=80&w=2000&auto=format&fit=crop" alt="Volcanic horizon over Aethelgard at twilight" class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover opacity-40" />
                    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-basalt-900 via-basalt-900/50 to-transparent"></div>
                    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-4xl space-y-3">
                        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ochre-desert">// ACT IV</span>
                        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-chalk uppercase font-bold">SEVERANCE</h2>
                        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-chalk/60">SECTOR 00 // BUREAU CONTROL CORE</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8 pt-12 story-prose">
                    <p>
                        Yara stood before the primary override panel in the central terminal room. On her screen, the countdown for Case #7709-M reached 00:04:12. Her hand rested over the manual purge switch—the button that would sever Kian's record permanently to protect the bureau's secrecy.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        A secondary window opened. It was a live comms relay from Warehouse 88. Nadia was on screen, looking directly into the vault camera. Behind Nadia, Teo and Priya were attempting to bypass the sub-silt vault lock.
                    </p>

                    <div class="my-8 p-4 sm:p-6 bg-black border border-amber-alert/60 rounded-sm font-mono text-xs space-y-3 text-chalk shadow-2xl">
                        <div class="flex justify-between border-b border-amber-alert/30 pb-2 text-amber-alert font-bold">
                            <span>[CRITICAL CHOICE DETECTED]</span>
                            <span>TIME REMAINING: 01:15</span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="text-chalk/80 leading-relaxed">
                            OPTION A: EXECUTE PURGE #7709-M — Preserve state ledger integrity. Erase Kian Vance.<br>
                            OPTION B: INITIATE CORE OVERLOAD — Release all stored memory coils into the public grid. Expose Relational Amortization. Risk total civic collapse.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <p>
                        Yara slowly reached forward, her fingers hovering between the two command keys. Outside the reinforced windows of Sector 00, the volcanic mist settled over Aethelgard's concrete towers.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pb-20 pt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between items-center gap-4 border-t border-basalt-700 font-mono text-xs">
